00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.300 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this is the town of Chippewa Falls  nestled along the Chippewa River in the  beautiful North Woods of Wisconsin  it's home to the lining Coogler family  and the jacob lining kugel Brewing  Company Brewer of Leinenkugel's summer  Shandy and one of the oldest breweries  in America so what's it take for one  family to keep the beer flowing for over  a hundred 50 years it's harder than  you'd think  our story begins in 1867 with a young  German immigrant a brewer named Jacob  line in Kouvola  I like to refer to my great-great  grandfather is no-neck lining for  centuries his family had been brewing  beer in Germany now he was looking to  make his mark in America in Chippewa  Falls Jacob discovered a source of pure  spring water which makes for a great  lager style beer he also discovered  2,500 thirsty Lumberjacks so he built a  brewery but brewing was hard work to  make ends meet he enlisted his family I  think the hardest worker out of that  family probably his wife Josephine  my great-great-great grandmother every  day she woke up at 3 a.m. to cook four  meals for the 20 brewery workers all  while raising four children a lot of  credit goes to Josephine the little  brewery prospered but then Jacob's  partner quit and Josephine died of  pneumonia aged 44 with a family to  support  Jacob had no choice but to keep ruing  and the people of Chippewa Falls loved  the beer so much they elected Jacob  mayor twice they continued to brew great  beer all the way up until the federal  government put us out of business in  1920 the United States bans the  manufacture and sale of alcohol  the dark days of prohibition descended  upon America and hundreds of breweries  vanished we had to stay in business and  had to stay together as a family to  survive prohibition they turned to  Jacobs daughter Susan electing her  president just six years after women won  the right to vote third cousin twice  removed you have to go back through a  family of lineage to find that she saved  Leinenkugel's by brewing soda pop and  mixers I got to believe that the mixers  were being mixed with something else  when Prohibition came to a close to  other line and kugel women Catherine  laning kugel and Rose Caspar came to the  rescue  they actually mortgage their homes to  get the brewing equipment back up and  operating not a lot of breweries came  out of prohibition mining kugels was  fortunate the reinvigorated brewery was  soon joined by Bill line and kugel a  marine returned from war bill my dad was  really the guy that expanded the paris'  footprint and into the North Woods of  Wisconsin bill had five children and  they helped out around the brewery as  bill hit the road spreading the gospel  of Leinenkugel's across the North Woods  he just went out and met the people put  a nice cold linings in her hands and  they loved the guy and that's what they  stuck with soon he had transformed  Leinenkugel's into a major Midwest  brewery but it wasn't enough small  Brewers were being priced out of  business by big Brewers who had invaded  their turf economics 101 folks back when  Leinenkugel's got started there were  nearly 4,000 breweries spread across  America by the late 70s only 89 remained  as Leinenkugel's became engulfed and the  price wars ash for Leinenkugel's it  received help from a fellow Wisconsin  brewery the 1987 that my dad received a  letter from Miller Brewing Company my  dad says I think they want us to buy  them  well it was obviously the other way  around Leinenkugel's kept its family  roots and bills three sons built upon  their father's legacy after partnering  with Miller Brewing Company we began to  develop different styles of beers that  we probably wouldn't have been able to  do on our own  [Music]  there's quite a feel so you'll have to  have some more film line and kugel  original honey vice berry vice canoe  paddler sunset wheat creamy dark big but  doppelbock what else lining Google's  summer Shandy  it wasn't until the development of  lighting Google's summer Shandy that we  decided to take lining Google's to the  rest of the country whether it's the  island of Manhattan New York or all the  way up to the great frontier of Alaska  that's pretty cool  [Music]  in 2017 Leinenkugel's celebrated 150  years as the pride of the Northwoods and  with time comes tradition line of kugels  and Chippewa Falls are synonymous when  you say Leinenkugel's you think chip  will fall Wisconsin when you say chip  will Falls Wisconsin you think line of  kugel beer  there's generations of Leinenkugel's  that have worked here at the brewery but  there's also been generations of other  families that have worked here and  continue to work here to this day our  hats off go to them as well it's a  legacy that was started in 1867 and  we're going to work really hard to  ensure that that legacy continues  [Music]  you  [Music]

